{"path":"3/library/fractions.html","title":"fractions — Rational numbers","description":"Source code: Lib/fractions.py","body":{"type":"document","children":[{"type":"anchor","id":"module-fractions"},{"type":"anchor","id":"fractions-rational-numbers"},{"type":"heading","level":1,"id":null,"children":[{"type":"inline_code","code":"fractions"},{"type":"text","value":" — Rational numbers"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Source code:"}]},{"type":"text","value":" "},{"type":"link","href":"https://github.com/python/cpython/tree/3.14/Lib/fractions.py","title":null,"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Lib/fractions.py"}]}]},{"type":"thematic_break"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The "},{"type":"inline_code","code":"fractions"},{"type":"text","value":" module provides support for rational number arithmetic."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"A Fraction instance can be constructed from a pair of rational numbers, from a single number, or from a string."}]},{"type":"definition_list","items":[{"id":"fractions.Fraction","term":[{"type":"emphasis","children":[{"type":"text","value":"class"},{"type":"text","value":" "}]},{"type":"text","value":"fractions.Fraction("},{"type":"emphasis","children":[{"type":"text","value":"numerator"},{"type":"text","value":"="},{"type":"text","value":"0"}]},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"emphasis","children":[{"type":"text","value":"denominator"},{"type":"text","value":"="},{"type":"text","value":"1"}]},{"type":"text","value":")"}],"definition":[]},{"id":null,"term":[{"type":"emphasis","children":[{"type":"text","value":"class"},{"type":"text","value":" "}]},{"type":"text","value":"fractions.Fraction("},{"type":"emphasis","children":[{"type":"text","value":"number"}]},{"type":"text","value":")"}],"definition":[]},{"id":null,"term":[{"type":"emphasis","children":[{"type":"text","value":"class"},{"type":"text","value":" "}]},{"type":"text","value":"fractions.Fraction("},{"type":"emphasis","children":[{"type":"text","value":"string"}]},{"type":"text","value":")"}],"definition":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The first version requires that "},{"type":"emphasis","children":[{"type":"text","value":"numerator"}]},{"type":"text","value":" and "},{"type":"emphasis","children":[{"type":"text","value":"denominator"}]},{"type":"text","value":" are instances of "},{"type":"link","href":"3/library/numbers.html#numbers.Rational","title":"numbers.Rational","children":[{"type":"inline_code","code":"numbers.Rational"}]},{"type":"text","value":" and returns a new "},{"type":"inline_code","code":"Fraction"},{"type":"text","value":" instance with a value equal to "},{"type":"inline_code","code":"numerator/denominator"},{"type":"text","value":". If "},{"type":"emphasis","children":[{"type":"text","value":"denominator"}]},{"type":"text","value":" is zero, it raises a "},{"type":"link","href":"3/library/exceptions.html#ZeroDivisionError","title":"ZeroDivisionError","children":[{"type":"inline_code","code":"ZeroDivisionError"}]},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The second version requires that "},{"type":"emphasis","children":[{"type":"text","value":"number"}]},{"type":"text","value":" is an instance of "},{"type":"link","href":"3/library/numbers.html#numbers.Rational","title":"numbers.Rational","children":[{"type":"inline_code","code":"numbers.Rational"}]},{"type":"text","value":" or has the "},{"type":"inline_code","code":"as_integer_ratio()"},{"type":"text","value":" method (this includes "},{"type":"link","href":"3/library/functions.html#float","title":"float","children":[{"type":"inline_code","code":"float"}]},{"type":"text","value":" and "},{"type":"link","href":"3/library/decimal.html#decimal.Decimal","title":"decimal.Decimal","children":[{"type":"inline_code","code":"decimal.Decimal"}]},{"type":"text","value":"). It returns a "},{"type":"inline_code","code":"Fraction"},{"type":"text","value":" instance with exactly the same value. Assumed, that the "},{"type":"inline_code","code":"as_integer_ratio()"},{"type":"text","value":" method returns a pair of coprime integers and last one is positive. Note that due to the usual issues with binary point (see "},{"type":"link","href":"3/tutorial/floatingpoint.html#tut-fp-issues","title":null,"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Floating-Point Arithmetic: Issues and Limitations"}]},{"type":"text","value":"), the argument to "},{"type":"inline_code","code":"Fraction(1.1)"},{"type":"text","value":" is not exactly equal to 11/10, and so "},{"type":"inline_code","code":"Fraction(1.1)"},{"type":"text","value":" does "},{"type":"emphasis","children":[{"type":"text","value":"not"}]},{"type":"text","value":" return "},{"type":"inline_code","code":"Fraction(11, 10)"},{"type":"text","value":" as one might expect. (But see the documentation for the "},{"type":"link","href":"3/library/fractions.html#fractions.Fraction.limit_denominator","title":"fractions.Fraction.limit_denominator","children":[{"type":"inline_code","code":"limit_denominator()"}]},{"type":"text","value":" method below.)"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The last version of the constructor expects a string. The usual form for this instance is:"}]},{"type":"code_block","language":"python","code":"[sign] numerator ['/' denominator]"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"where the optional "},{"type":"inline_code","code":"sign"},{"type":"text","value":" may be either ‘+’ or ‘-’ and "},{"type":"inline_code","code":"numerator"},{"type":"text","value":" and "},{"type":"inline_code","code":"denominator"},{"type":"text","value":" (if present) are strings of decimal digits (underscores may be used to delimit digits as with integral literals in code). In addition, any string that represents a finite value and is accepted by the "},{"type":"link","href":"3/library/functions.html#float","title":"float","children":[{"type":"inline_code","code":"float"}]},{"type":"text","value":" constructor is also accepted by the "},{"type":"inline_code","code":"Fraction"},{"type":"text","value":" constructor. In either form the input string may also have leading and/or trailing whitespace. Here are some examples:"}]},{"type":"code_block","language":"python","code":">>> from fractions import Fraction\n>>> Fraction(16, -10)\nFraction(-8, 5)\n>>> Fraction(123)\nFraction(123, 1)\n>>> Fraction()\nFraction(0, 1)\n>>> Fraction('3/7')\nFraction(3, 7)\n>>> Fraction(' -3/7 ')\nFraction(-3, 7)\n>>> Fraction('1.414213 \\t\\n')\nFraction(1414213, 1000000)\n>>> Fraction('-.125')\nFraction(-1, 8)\n>>> Fraction('7e-6')\nFraction(7, 1000000)\n>>> Fraction(2.25)\nFraction(9, 4)\n>>> Fraction(1.1)\nFraction(2476979795053773, 2251799813685248)\n>>> from decimal import Decimal\n>>> Fraction(Decimal('1.1'))\nFraction(11, 10)"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The "},{"type":"inline_code","code":"Fraction"},{"type":"text","value":" class inherits from the abstract base class "},{"type":"link","href":"3/library/numbers.html#numbers.Rational","title":"numbers.Rational","children":[{"type":"inline_code","code":"numbers.Rational"}]},{"type":"text","value":", and implements all of the methods and operations from that class. "},{"type":"inline_code","code":"Fraction"},{"type":"text","value":" instances are "},{"type":"link","href":"https://docs.python.org/3/glossary.html#term-hashable","title":null,"children":[{"type":"text","value":"hashable"}]},{"type":"text","value":", and should be treated as immutable. In addition, "},{"type":"inline_code","code":"Fraction"},{"type":"text","value":" has the following properties and methods:"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Changed in version 3.2: The "},{"type":"inline_code","code":"Fraction"},{"type":"text","value":" constructor now accepts "},{"type":"link","href":"3/library/functions.html#float","title":"float","children":[{"type":"inline_code","code":"float"}]},{"type":"text","value":" and "},{"type":"link","href":"3/library/decimal.html#decimal.Decimal","title":"decimal.Decimal","children":[{"type":"inline_code","code":"decimal.Decimal"}]},{"type":"text","value":" instances."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Changed in version 3.9: The "},{"type":"link","href":"3/library/math.html#math.gcd","title":"math.gcd","children":[{"type":"inline_code","code":"math.gcd()"}]},{"type":"text","value":" function is now used to normalize the "},{"type":"emphasis","children":[{"type":"text","value":"numerator"}]},{"type":"text","value":" and "},{"type":"emphasis","children":[{"type":"text","value":"denominator"}]},{"type":"text","value":". "},{"type":"inline_code","code":"math.gcd()"},{"type":"text","value":" always returns an "},{"type":"link","href":"3/library/functions.html#int","title":"int","children":[{"type":"inline_code","code":"int"}]},{"type":"text","value":" type. Previously, the GCD type depended on "},{"type":"emphasis","children":[{"type":"text","value":"numerator"}]},{"type":"text","value":" and "},{"type":"emphasis","children":[{"type":"text","value":"denominator"}]},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Changed in version 3.11: Underscores are now permitted when creating a "},{"type":"inline_code","code":"Fraction"},{"type":"text","value":" instance from a string, following "},{"type":"anchor","id":"index-1"},{"type":"link","href":"https://peps.python.org/pep-0515/","title":null,"children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"PEP 515"}]}]},{"type":"text","value":" rules."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Changed in version 3.11: "},{"type":"inline_code","code":"Fraction"},{"type":"text","value":" implements "},{"type":"inline_code","code":"__int__"},{"type":"text","value":" now to satisfy "},{"type":"inline_code","code":"typing.SupportsInt"},{"type":"text","value":" instance checks."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Changed in version 3.12: Space is allowed around the slash for string inputs: "},{"type":"inline_code","code":"Fraction('2 / 3')"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Changed in version 3.12: "},{"type":"inline_code","code":"Fraction"},{"type":"text","value":" instances now support float-style formatting, with presentation types "},{"type":"inline_code","code":"\"e\""},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inline_code","code":"\"E\""},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inline_code","code":"\"f\""},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inline_code","code":"\"F\""},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inline_code","code":"\"g\""},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inline_code","code":"\"G\""},{"type":"text","value":" and "},{"type":"inline_code","code":"\"%\"\""},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Changed in version 3.13: Formatting of "},{"type":"inline_code","code":"Fraction"},{"type":"text","value":" instances without a presentation type now supports fill, alignment, sign handling, minimum width and grouping."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Changed in version 3.14: The "},{"type":"inline_code","code":"Fraction"},{"type":"text","value":" constructor now accepts any objects with the "},{"type":"inline_code","code":"as_integer_ratio()"},{"type":"text","value":" method."}]},{"type":"definition_list","items":[{"id":"fractions.Fraction.numerator","term":[{"type":"text","value":"numerator"}],"definition":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Numerator of the Fraction in lowest term."}]}]}]},{"type":"definition_list","items":[{"id":"fractions.Fraction.denominator","term":[{"type":"text","value":"denominator"}],"definition":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Denominator of the Fraction in lowest terms. Guaranteed to be positive."}]}]}]},{"type":"definition_list","items":[{"id":"fractions.Fraction.as_integer_ratio","term":[{"type":"text","value":"as_integer_ratio()"}],"definition":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Return a tuple of two integers, whose ratio is equal to the original Fraction. The ratio is in lowest terms and has a positive denominator."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Added in version 3.8."}]}]}]},{"type":"definition_list","items":[{"id":"fractions.Fraction.is_integer","term":[{"type":"text","value":"is_integer()"}],"definition":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Return "},{"type":"inline_code","code":"True"},{"type":"text","value":" if the Fraction is an integer."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Added in version 3.12."}]}]}]},{"type":"definition_list","items":[{"id":"fractions.Fraction.from_float","term":[{"type":"emphasis","children":[{"type":"text","value":"classmethod"},{"type":"text","value":" "}]},{"type":"text","value":"from_float("},{"type":"emphasis","children":[{"type":"text","value":"f"}]},{"type":"text","value":")"}],"definition":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Alternative constructor which only accepts instances of "},{"type":"link","href":"3/library/functions.html#float","title":"float","children":[{"type":"inline_code","code":"float"}]},{"type":"text","value":" or "},{"type":"link","href":"3/library/numbers.html#numbers.Integral","title":"numbers.Integral","children":[{"type":"inline_code","code":"numbers.Integral"}]},{"type":"text","value":". Beware that "},{"type":"inline_code","code":"Fraction.from_float(0.3)"},{"type":"text","value":" is not the same value as "},{"type":"inline_code","code":"Fraction(3, 10)"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"admonition","kind":"note","title":"Note","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"From Python 3.2 onwards, you can also construct a "},{"type":"inline_code","code":"Fraction"},{"type":"text","value":" instance directly from a "},{"type":"link","href":"3/library/functions.html#float","title":"float","children":[{"type":"inline_code","code":"float"}]},{"type":"text","value":"."}]}]}]}]},{"type":"definition_list","items":[{"id":"fractions.Fraction.from_decimal","term":[{"type":"emphasis","children":[{"type":"text","value":"classmethod"},{"type":"text","value":" "}]},{"type":"text","value":"from_decimal("},{"type":"emphasis","children":[{"type":"text","value":"dec"}]},{"type":"text","value":")"}],"definition":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Alternative constructor which only accepts instances of "},{"type":"link","href":"3/library/decimal.html#decimal.Decimal","title":"decimal.Decimal","children":[{"type":"inline_code","code":"decimal.Decimal"}]},{"type":"text","value":" or "},{"type":"link","href":"3/library/numbers.html#numbers.Integral","title":"numbers.Integral","children":[{"type":"inline_code","code":"numbers.Integral"}]},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"admonition","kind":"note","title":"Note","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"From Python 3.2 onwards, you can also construct a "},{"type":"inline_code","code":"Fraction"},{"type":"text","value":" instance directly from a "},{"type":"link","href":"3/library/decimal.html#decimal.Decimal","title":"decimal.Decimal","children":[{"type":"inline_code","code":"decimal.Decimal"}]},{"type":"text","value":" instance."}]}]}]}]},{"type":"definition_list","items":[{"id":"fractions.Fraction.from_number","term":[{"type":"emphasis","children":[{"type":"text","value":"classmethod"},{"type":"text","value":" "}]},{"type":"text","value":"from_number("},{"type":"emphasis","children":[{"type":"text","value":"number"}]},{"type":"text","value":")"}],"definition":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Alternative constructor which only accepts instances of "},{"type":"link","href":"3/library/numbers.html#numbers.Integral","title":"numbers.Integral","children":[{"type":"inline_code","code":"numbers.Integral"}]},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"link","href":"3/library/numbers.html#numbers.Rational","title":"numbers.Rational","children":[{"type":"inline_code","code":"numbers.Rational"}]},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"link","href":"3/library/functions.html#float","title":"float","children":[{"type":"inline_code","code":"float"}]},{"type":"text","value":" or "},{"type":"link","href":"3/library/decimal.html#decimal.Decimal","title":"decimal.Decimal","children":[{"type":"inline_code","code":"decimal.Decimal"}]},{"type":"text","value":", and objects with the "},{"type":"inline_code","code":"as_integer_ratio()"},{"type":"text","value":" method, but not strings."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Added in version 3.14."}]}]}]},{"type":"definition_list","items":[{"id":"fractions.Fraction.limit_denominator","term":[{"type":"text","value":"limit_denominator("},{"type":"emphasis","children":[{"type":"text","value":"max_denominator"},{"type":"text","value":"="},{"type":"text","value":"1000000"}]},{"type":"text","value":")"}],"definition":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Finds and returns the closest "},{"type":"inline_code","code":"Fraction"},{"type":"text","value":" to "},{"type":"inline_code","code":"self"},{"type":"text","value":" that has denominator at most max_denominator. This method is useful for finding rational approximations to a given floating-point number:"}]},{"type":"code_block","language":null,"code":">>> from fractions import Fraction\n>>> Fraction('3.1415926535897932').limit_denominator(1000)\nFraction(355, 113)"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"or for recovering a rational number that’s represented as a float:"}]},{"type":"code_block","language":null,"code":">>> from math import pi, cos\n>>> Fraction(cos(pi/3))\nFraction(4503599627370497, 9007199254740992)\n>>> Fraction(cos(pi/3)).limit_denominator()\nFraction(1, 2)\n>>> Fraction(1.1).limit_denominator()\nFraction(11, 10)"}]}]},{"type":"definition_list","items":[{"id":"fractions.Fraction.__floor__","term":[{"type":"text","value":"__floor__()"}],"definition":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Returns the greatest "},{"type":"link","href":"3/library/functions.html#int","title":"int","children":[{"type":"inline_code","code":"int"}]},{"type":"text","value":" "},{"type":"inline_code","code":"<= self"},{"type":"text","value":". This method can also be accessed through the "},{"type":"link","href":"3/library/math.html#math.floor","title":"math.floor","children":[{"type":"inline_code","code":"math.floor()"}]},{"type":"text","value":" function:"}]},{"type":"code_block","language":null,"code":">>> from math import floor\n>>> floor(Fraction(355, 113))\n3"}]}]},{"type":"definition_list","items":[{"id":"fractions.Fraction.__ceil__","term":[{"type":"text","value":"__ceil__()"}],"definition":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Returns the least "},{"type":"link","href":"3/library/functions.html#int","title":"int","children":[{"type":"inline_code","code":"int"}]},{"type":"text","value":" "},{"type":"inline_code","code":">= self"},{"type":"text","value":". This method can also be accessed through the "},{"type":"link","href":"3/library/math.html#math.ceil","title":"math.ceil","children":[{"type":"inline_code","code":"math.ceil()"}]},{"type":"text","value":" function."}]}]}]},{"type":"definition_list","items":[{"id":"fractions.Fraction.__round__","term":[{"type":"text","value":"__round__()"}],"definition":[]},{"id":null,"term":[{"type":"text","value":"__round__("},{"type":"emphasis","children":[{"type":"text","value":"ndigits"}]},{"type":"text","value":")"}],"definition":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The first version returns the nearest "},{"type":"link","href":"3/library/functions.html#int","title":"int","children":[{"type":"inline_code","code":"int"}]},{"type":"text","value":" to "},{"type":"inline_code","code":"self"},{"type":"text","value":", rounding half to even. The second version rounds "},{"type":"inline_code","code":"self"},{"type":"text","value":" to the nearest multiple of "},{"type":"inline_code","code":"Fraction(1, 10**ndigits)"},{"type":"text","value":" (logically, if "},{"type":"inline_code","code":"ndigits"},{"type":"text","value":" is negative), again rounding half toward even. This method can also be accessed through the "},{"type":"link","href":"3/library/functions.html#round","title":"round","children":[{"type":"inline_code","code":"round()"}]},{"type":"text","value":" function."}]}]}]},{"type":"definition_list","items":[{"id":"fractions.Fraction.__format__","term":[{"type":"text","value":"__format__("},{"type":"emphasis","children":[{"type":"text","value":"format_spec"}]},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"emphasis","children":[{"type":"text","value":"/"}]},{"type":"text","value":")"}],"definition":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Provides support for formatting of "},{"type":"inline_code","code":"Fraction"},{"type":"text","value":" instances via the "},{"type":"link","href":"3/library/stdtypes.html#str.format","title":"str.format","children":[{"type":"inline_code","code":"str.format()"}]},{"type":"text","value":" method, the "},{"type":"link","href":"3/library/functions.html#format","title":"format","children":[{"type":"inline_code","code":"format()"}]},{"type":"text","value":" built-in function, or "},{"type":"link","href":"https://docs.python.org/3/reference/lexical_analysis.html#f-strings","title":null,"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Formatted string literals"}]},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"If the "},{"type":"inline_code","code":"format_spec"},{"type":"text","value":" format specification string does not end with one of the presentation types "},{"type":"inline_code","code":"'e'"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inline_code","code":"'E'"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inline_code","code":"'f'"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inline_code","code":"'F'"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inline_code","code":"'g'"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inline_code","code":"'G'"},{"type":"text","value":" or "},{"type":"inline_code","code":"'%'"},{"type":"text","value":" then formatting follows the general rules for fill, alignment, sign handling, minimum width, and grouping as described in the "},{"type":"link","href":"3/library/string.html#formatspec","title":null,"children":[{"type":"text","value":"format specification mini-language"}]},{"type":"text","value":". The “alternate form” flag "},{"type":"inline_code","code":"'#'"},{"type":"text","value":" is supported: if present, it forces the output string to always include an explicit denominator, even when the value being formatted is an exact integer. The zero-fill flag "},{"type":"inline_code","code":"'0'"},{"type":"text","value":" is not supported."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"If the "},{"type":"inline_code","code":"format_spec"},{"type":"text","value":" format specification string ends with one of the presentation types "},{"type":"inline_code","code":"'e'"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inline_code","code":"'E'"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inline_code","code":"'f'"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inline_code","code":"'F'"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inline_code","code":"'g'"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inline_code","code":"'G'"},{"type":"text","value":" or "},{"type":"inline_code","code":"'%'"},{"type":"text","value":" then formatting follows the rules outlined for the "},{"type":"link","href":"3/library/functions.html#float","title":"float","children":[{"type":"inline_code","code":"float"}]},{"type":"text","value":" type in the "},{"type":"link","href":"3/library/string.html#formatspec","title":null,"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Format specification mini-language"}]},{"type":"text","value":" section."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Here are some examples:"}]},{"type":"code_block","language":"python","code":">>> from fractions import Fraction\n>>> format(Fraction(103993, 33102), '_')\n'103_993/33_102'\n>>> format(Fraction(1, 7), '.^+10')\n'...+1/7...'\n>>> format(Fraction(3, 1), '')\n'3'\n>>> format(Fraction(3, 1), '#')\n'3/1'\n>>> format(Fraction(1, 7), '.40g')\n'0.1428571428571428571428571428571428571429'\n>>> format(Fraction('1234567.855'), '_.2f')\n'1_234_567.86'\n>>> f\"{Fraction(355, 113):*>20.6e}\"\n'********3.141593e+00'\n>>> old_price, new_price = 499, 672\n>>> \"{:.2%} price increase\".format(Fraction(new_price, old_price) - 1)\n'34.67% price increase'"}]}]}]}]},{"type":"admonition","kind":"seealso","title":"See also","children":[{"type":"definition_list","items":[{"id":null,"term":[{"type":"text","value":"Module "},{"type":"link","href":"3/library/numbers.html#module-numbers","title":"numbers: Numeric abstract base classes (Complex, Real, Integral, etc.).","children":[{"type":"inline_code","code":"numbers"}]}],"definition":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The abstract base classes making up the numeric tower."}]}]}]}]}]}}
